    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Tests the valid value ranges that {@link Symmetry454Chronology} reports for each supported {@code ChronoField}. <p>The Symmetry454 calendar is a leap-week calendar: every month has 4 weeks (28 days), except February, May, August and November, which have 5 weeks (35 days). Leap years add an extra week to December, so the longer maxima below (e.g. 35 days, 53 weeks, 371 days) reflect the longest months/years rather than the common case."
   },
   {
    "id": "i2",
    "kind": "LineComment",
    "lines": [
     38,
     38
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Week-based fields: a week is always 7 days."
   },
   {
    "id": "i3",
    "kind": "LineComment",
    "lines": [
     43,
     43
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Weeks within a month: 4 in a normal month, 5 in a long (or leap-extended) month."
   },
   {
